{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"aidlcgroup0001","type":"group","x":960,"y":-620,"width":1360,"height":1360,"color":"4","label":"⑤ AIDLC docs  ·  Inception → Requirements → Construction"},
		{"id":"grouproutes01","type":"group","x":-1160,"y":-600,"width":1960,"height":580,"color":"5","label":"① Route templates  ·  src/app/single-brand/"},
		{"id":"r1file00000001","type":"file","file":"hearst-design-system/src/app/single-brand/page.tsx","x":-1040,"y":-520,"width":420,"height":90},
		{"id":"r1desc00000001","type":"text","text":"**Index / landing**\n`/single-brand`\n\nLists the pilot brands from `SINGLE_BRANDS`; each card links to that brand's home. Static, no reader.","x":-1040,"y":-365,"width":420,"height":200},
		{"id":"r2file00000001","type":"file","file":"hearst-design-system/src/app/single-brand/[brandSlug]/page.tsx","x":-300,"y":-520,"width":420,"height":90},
		{"id":"r2desc00000001","type":"text","text":"**Brand home (river)**\n`/single-brand/[brandSlug]`\n\nRenders `HomePageTemplate` with `liveFeedMode=\"replace\"`, the brand's live feed, masthead override + theme. `force-dynamic`, `forceDestinationRiver`.","x":-300,"y":-325,"width":420,"height":200},
		{"id":"r3file00000001","type":"file","file":"hearst-design-system/src/app/single-brand/[brandSlug]/article/[storyId]/page.tsx","x":340,"y":-520,"width":420,"height":90},
		{"id":"r3desc00000001","type":"text","text":"**Article reader**\n`/single-brand/[brandSlug]/article/[storyId]`\n\nSame template, opens its built-in modal reader on the story via `initialOpenStoryId` (with infinite \"up next\"). A missing/stale id degrades gracefully to brand home.","x":340,"y":-325,"width":420,"height":200},
		{"id":"enginefile001","type":"file","file":"hearst-design-system/src/components/home-page.tsx","x":-690,"y":960,"width":460,"height":90},
		{"id":"datafile00001","type":"file","file":"hearst-design-system/src/lib/personalize-live-feed.ts","x":370,"y":960,"width":460,"height":90},
		{"id":"enginedesc001","type":"text","text":"**③ Rendering engine**\n`src/components/home-page.tsx`\n\nThe real Hearst+ `HomePageTemplate`: cross-brand river + full-screen modal reader. Constrained to one brand purely through props.","x":-690,"y":1065,"width":460,"height":180},
		{"id":"datadesc00001","type":"text","text":"**④ Content source**\n`src/lib/personalize-live-feed.ts`\n\nPersonalize live feed, filtered to the brand; falls back to the static snapshot when the API is unavailable — always resolves to brand-scoped stories.","x":370,"y":1065,"width":460,"height":180},
		{"id":"docsfile000001","type":"file","file":"hearst-design-system/AIDLC-docs/vision-single-brand-destinations.md","x":-1080,"y":280,"width":460,"height":102,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"docsdesc000001","type":"text","text":"**Vision** · Inception input\nBrownfield change: reuse `HomePageTemplate`, do **not** build a new layout. Current state, what we add, MVP boundary (3 pilot brands). Feeds the docs on the right →\n\n📄 [[vision-single-brand-destinations]]","x":-1080,"y":399,"width":460,"height":181,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"title0000000001","type":"text","text":"# Hearst+ Single-Brand Templates\n\nThe Hearst+ river + modal-reader experience scoped to **one brand at a time** — same layout, but the brand supplies its own feed, theme, and masthead. Pilot cohort: **Delish · Cosmopolitan · Redbook**.","x":-1160,"y":-840,"width":860,"height":130,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"usfile00000001","type":"file","file":"hearst-design-system/AIDLC-docs/user-stories-single-brand-destinations.md","x":1020,"y":-540,"width":500,"height":90,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"usdesc00000001","type":"text","text":"**User stories** · Requirements Analysis\n\nRefines the vision into testable requirements. Personas (Anonymous / Returning Reader, Brand Editorial, DS Maintainer), epics, Given/When/Then acceptance, and status tags (✅ done · 🔶 partial · ⬜ planned). MVP scope = the 3 pilot brands.\n\n📄 [[user-stories-single-brand-destinations]]","x":1020,"y":-435,"width":500,"height":225,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"tefile00000001","type":"file","file":"hearst-design-system/AIDLC-docs/tech-env-single-brand-destinations.md","x":1020,"y":-150,"width":500,"height":90,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"tedesc00000001","type":"text","text":"**Technical environment** · Construction constraints\n\nThe existing stack that must be preserved: TS 5 (strict), Next 16 (App Router / RSC), React 19, Tailwind v4, Style Dictionary tokens, Storybook, Netlify + Blobs, Vitest / Playwright. New code fits established patterns — no new frameworks.\n\n📄 [[tech-env-single-brand-destinations]]","x":1020,"y":-45,"width":500,"height":225,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"secfile0000001","type":"file","file":"hearst-design-system/AIDLC-docs/security-compliance-matrix.md","x":1020,"y":240,"width":500,"height":90,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"secdesc0000001","type":"text","text":"**Security compliance matrix** · companion to tech-env\n\nMaps the app to OWASP Top 10 (2021) with a status per category (Addressed / Gap / N/A / Deferred). Flags open gaps: CSP, the `http` image host, dependency scanning, SSRF allow-list. PCI / HIPAA / NIST marked N/A with justification.\n\n📄 [[security-compliance-matrix]]","x":1020,"y":345,"width":500,"height":225,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"legend00000001","type":"text","text":"**Legend** — 🟩 **Project artifacts**: the docs this feature actually uses (the 🟩 Vision doc sits on the left, wired into the code).  ·  🟧 **Method guides & references**: how to write / govern each doc. AIDLC order flows top → bottom: Vision → User stories → Tech env → Security.","x":1020,"y":600,"width":1240,"height":80},
		{"id":"tgfile00000001","type":"file","file":"hearst-design-system/AIDLC-docs/technical-environment-guide.md","x":1760,"y":-150,"width":500,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"tgdesc00000001","type":"text","text":"**Technical Environment guide** (method)\n\nHow to write the Tech-Env doc: tooling, standards, constraints, NFRs. Greenfield-vs-brownfield guidance. A reusable template, not project-specific.\n\n📄 [[technical-environment-guide]]","x":1760,"y":-45,"width":500,"height":225,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dsfile00000001","type":"file","file":"hearst-design-system/AIDLC-docs/DESIGN-SYSTEM-SPEC.md","x":1760,"y":240,"width":500,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"dsdesc00000001","type":"text","text":"**Design System spec** (reference)\n\nRepository specification: authority table (canonical `tokens/`, production behavior, Storybook), token architecture, component contract. Figma / Pencil are downstream consumers — not sources of truth.\n\n📄 [[DESIGN-SYSTEM-SPEC]]","x":1760,"y":345,"width":500,"height":225,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"vgdesc00000001","type":"text","text":"**Vision Document guide** (method)\n\nHow to write the Vision Document — the Inception input: executive summary, business goals, scope boundaries. A reusable template, not project-specific.\n\n📄 [[vision-document-guide]]","x":1760,"y":-435,"width":500,"height":225,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"vgfile00000001","type":"file","file":"hearst-design-system/AIDLC-docs/vision-document-guide.md","x":1760,"y":-540,"width":500,"height":90,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"adapterfile01","type":"file","file":"hearst-design-system/src/templates/single-brand-feed.ts","x":-230,"y":280,"width":460,"height":90},
		{"id":"adapterdesc01","type":"text","text":"**② Shared adapter**\n`src/templates/single-brand-feed.ts`\n\n- `SINGLE_BRANDS` — pilot cohort\n- `getSingleBrandLiveFeed()` — brand-scoped feed\n- `getSingleBrandMasthead()` — brand logo\n- `isSingleBrand()` / `getSingleBrandName()`\n\nNo new layout — just wires props into the existing template.","x":-230,"y":400,"width":460,"height":240,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"phgroup000001","type":"group","x":-2240,"y":-600,"width":960,"height":1100,"color":"6","label":"AIDLC phases (reference)"},
		{"id":"phintro000001","type":"text","text":"## AI Development Life Cycle\n\nEach phase's output feeds the next, reducing ambiguity **before** any code is written. Docs on the right are the artifacts of each phase.","x":-2200,"y":-540,"width":880,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"phinc00000001","type":"text","text":"### 1 · Inception  —  *why & what*\n\nDefine business goals, target outcomes, and scope. Decide what's in the MVP vs. deferred.\n\n**Produces:** the Vision → [[vision-single-brand-destinations]]","x":-2200,"y":-410,"width":880,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"phreq00000001","type":"text","text":"### 2 · Requirements Analysis  —  *who & when-then*\n\nRefine the vision into testable requirements: personas, epics, Given/When/Then acceptance criteria.\n\n**Produces:** User stories → [[user-stories-single-brand-destinations]]","x":-2200,"y":-200,"width":880,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"phcon00000001","type":"text","text":"### 3 · Construction  —  *how it's built*\n\nGenerate/write the code within fixed technical + security constraints, so the AI doesn't invent new patterns or wrong assumptions.\n\n**Binds to:** [[tech-env-single-brand-destinations]] · [[security-compliance-matrix]]\n**Produces:** the code — routes → adapter → engine → data.","x":-2200,"y":10,"width":880,"height":230,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"phops00000001","type":"text","text":"### 4 · Operations  —  *run & monitor*  (future)\n\nDeploy, observe, and iterate. Not yet captured as an AIDLC-doc artifact in this repo.","x":-2200,"y":270,"width":880,"height":150,"color":"6"}
	],
